{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Extraction guard",
  "description": "Kiro IDE copy of extraction-guard.json: when the lease extractor or the coverage check is edited, keep every quote verbatim and every unreadable clause a \"can't tell\", and ask for an extraction test.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "src/lease/extract.ts",
      "src/lease/coverage.ts"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "You just edited the lease extractor or the coverage check (src/lease/extract.ts or src/lease/coverage.ts). Before continuing: every fact's quote must be the exact sentence from the clause it cites, so verifyFacts still keeps it; when a sentence is ambiguous, propose no fact rather than guess; a clause that has a predicate's cue words but no verified fact for it must be recorded as unread, so the answer is \"Can't tell\" and never \"the lease says nothing\"; and the three sample leases must still produce no unread entries and exactly the fact lists in tests/unit/extract.test.ts. Add or update an extraction test in tests/unit/extract.test.ts for each wording you add or change, and a test in tests/unit/coverage.test.ts for each cue change. Then run `npm test` and fix the code, not the test, unless .kiro/specs/proof-chain-answers/requirements.md says the test is wrong."
  }
}
